// Vector.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Type Constructors — Functions That Return Types
// Grammar: type-constructor-primary, type-constructor-binding
//
// A type constructor is a function that takes a value or a type and RETURNS A
// TYPE. Here the input is a size and the result depends on it, which is what
// makes the result a dependent type.
//
//     Vector(3)  ->  co.lang.int->([3])
//     Vector(4)  ->  co.lang.int->([4])
//
// The binding is a type expression, so the declaration ends with a semicolon.
//
// The name is written out rather than inferred with `_`. Filename inference
// works through `declaration-name`, but a type constructor's name position is
// `function-name = identifier | lifecycle-name`, and a lone `_` is a
// contextual token, never an identifier. The same applies to macros and other
// annotated function primaries.

_ co.lang.unit = {
Vector(n co.lang.int)->(co.lang.dependentType) =
    co.lang.int->([n]);
}
